# Alembic Migrations — CANONICAL Migration Path

**Alembic is THE canonical migration system for SupremeAI.** All new tables and
schema changes MUST ship as Alembic revisions in `versions/` — raw SQL files
(e.g. the archived trees under `backend/database/migrations/legacy/`) are no
longer an accepted way to change the schema.

## Workflow

```bash
cd backend
alembic upgrade head                                  # apply all pending migrations
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"      # create a new revision
alembic history                                       # view migration history
alembic downgrade -1                                  # rollback one revision
```

## Rules

1. **Every new table MUST get an Alembic revision.** No exceptions — including
   "temporary" tables and seed-critical schema.
2. **One linear history:** give each revision a descriptive slug; if two
   branches both add revisions, create a merge revision (see
   `cb8d8501f289_merge_heads.py` / `h3i4j5k6l7m8_merge_heads.py`).
3. **Downgrade path:** write a real `downgrade()` (or an explicit
   `pass` + comment if truly irreversible) for every revision.
4. **Raw SQL is archived, not deleted:** pre-Alembic SQL lives read-only under
   `backend/database/migrations/legacy/` (see its README for per-file
   dispositions). Do not execute it as part of any workflow.

Generic single-database configuration.
